    "ilya": "anja"
  },
  "labels": {
    "anya": "Макс",
    "ilya": "Илья"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "At Claude Monet, two friends discuss a woman's intelligence and career in the restaurant business. Max and Ilya are talking about a very impressive woman they know. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В смысле?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "В прямом смысле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она умная и красивая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я согласен с тобой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она закончила университет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она изучала управление ресторанами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень престижное образование.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "А потом она здесь работала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она работала в нашем ресторане?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Да, она была менеджером.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не знал об этом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она очень талантливая девушка.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Smart and Beautiful line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В смысле?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In what sense?' There is no question word here — in Russian, rising intonation on 'sense' is enough to make it a question. And Ilya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "В прямом смысле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In the direct sense.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'straight' directly with 'sense', combining 'straight' with 'sense'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она умная и красивая.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She is smart and beautiful.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be', connecting 'it' directly with 'pretty'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я согласен с тобой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I agree with you.' Max delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'agreed'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она закончила университет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She finished the university.' Ilya uses the perfective verb meaning 'finished' to focus on the single completed result, pairing it with 'university'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она изучала управление ресторанами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She studied restaurant management.' Ilya chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'to study' for the ongoing action, followed by 'headquarters' and 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень престижное образование.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a very prestigious education.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'very much' directly with 'prestigious', combining 'very much' with 'prestigious' and 'education'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "А потом она здесь работала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And then she worked here.' Notice how the verb meaning 'worked' takes the feminine past-tense ending '-a' here.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она работала в нашем ресторане?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She worked in our restaurant?' Max turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'worked', followed by 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Да, она была менеджером.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, she was a manager.' Ilya chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'was' for the ongoing action, followed by 'manager'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не знал об этом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not know about this.' Max delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'knew'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она очень талантливая девушка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She is a very talented girl.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'it' straight to 'girlfriend'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В смысле?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "В прямом смысле.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Она умная и красивая.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
